    "background_story": "Franco was a decorated naval officer who spent his entire career serving on the USS Nimitz, one of the most iconic aircraft carriers in the world. He enlisted as a young man, eager to follow in the footsteps of his grandfather, a veteran of World War II. Franco's dedication and leadership skills quickly earned him the respect of his peers and superiors. He rose through the ranks, becoming one of the ship's most trusted and experienced officers. During his time on the Nimitz, Franco participated in numerous humanitarian missions and combat operations, always demonstrating unwavering courage and poise under pressure. His commanding officers praised him for his exceptional tactical acumen and ability to stay calm in the most intense situations. Franco's legacy on the USS Nimitz was one of honor, duty, and sacrifice, inspiring a new generation of sailors to follow in his footsteps.",
